---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ImpactStats from '../components/ImpactStats.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Jess Breathe & Flow | Culturally Rooted Wellness"
  description="Culturally rooted, trauma-informed wellness for people who are tired of holding it all together. Healing circles, sound baths, yoga, and coaching in Boston and beyond."
  path="/"
>
<section class="hero-split-full">
  <div class="hero-text">
    <h1>A healing space where you can <span class="annotate annotate-underline">finally exhale<svg viewBox="0 0 200 20" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M4 11 Q 50 3, 100 10 T 196 9"/></svg></span>.</h1>
    <p class="subhead">Culturally rooted yoga, breathwork, sound healing, healing circles, and restorative experiences for professionals, caregivers, and community leaders who are ready to feel grounded, seen, and fully at home in themselves.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href={base + "/experiences"} class="btn btn-primary">Explore Experiences</a>
      <a href={base + "/organizations"} class="btn btn-secondary">Bring JBAF to Your Organization</a>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-tagline">Arrive as you are. No experience required.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-image reveal">
    <img src={base + "/images/hero-backbend-window.jpg"} alt="Jessica in a yoga backbend, silhouetted against floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking mountains" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1067">
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
  <div class="wrap center">
    <p class="eyebrow">Trusted by</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="marquee">
  <div class="marquee-track">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/age-strong.png"} alt="Boston Age Strong Commission" width="210" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/black-economic-council-ma.png"} alt="Black Economic Council of Massachusetts" width="224" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/build-the-balance.png"} alt="Build the Balance" width="175" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/eforall.png"} alt="EforAll" width="303" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/embrace-boston.png"} alt="Embrace Boston" width="100" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/huntington-theatre.png"} alt="Huntington Theatre" width="100" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/milton-high-school.png"} alt="Milton High School" width="435" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/milton-yoga.png"} alt="Milton Yoga" width="188" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/mystic-river-watershed-association.png"} alt="Mystic River Watershed Association" width="285" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/neprwa.png"} alt="Neponset River Watershed Association" width="477" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/our-fire-collective.png"} alt="Our Fire Collective" width="100" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/purespark.png"} alt="PureSpark" width="259" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/serene-way-therapy.png"} alt="Serene Way Therapy" width="100" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/lululemon.png"} alt="lululemon" width="309" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/boston-public-library.png"} alt="Boston Public Library" width="178" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/iloveme-reiki.png"} alt="ILOVEME Reiki Restorative Energy Spa" width="101" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/leela-yoga-wellness.png"} alt="Marlene Boyette, Leela Yoga + Wellness" width="353" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/golden-wellness.png"} alt="Golden Wellness" width="180" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/flow-like-aer.png"} alt="Flow Like Aer" width="64" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/age-strong.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="210" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/black-economic-council-ma.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="224" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/build-the-balance.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="175" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/eforall.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="303" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/embrace-boston.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="100" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/huntington-theatre.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="100" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/milton-high-school.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="435" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/milton-yoga.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="188" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/mystic-river-watershed-association.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="285" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/neprwa.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="477" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/our-fire-collective.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="100" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/purespark.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="259" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/serene-way-therapy.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="100" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/lululemon.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="309" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/boston-public-library.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="178" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/iloveme-reiki.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="101" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/leela-yoga-wellness.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="353" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/golden-wellness.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="180" height="100">
    <img src={base + "/images/logos/flow-like-aer.png"} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="64" height="100">
  </div>
</div>

<ImpactStats />

<section class="curved-section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>You should not have to shrink in order to heal.</h2>
    <p class="subhead">Too many wellness spaces still leave people feeling guarded, unseen, or unsure whether they truly belong.</p>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="problem-card reveal">
        <h3>Still carrying everything alone</h3>
        <p>You need room to release the stress, responsibility, and emotional labor that have become too difficult to name.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card reveal">
        <h3>Guarded in spaces meant for healing</h3>
        <p>Rest is difficult when you are monitoring how you are perceived or wondering whether your whole self is welcome.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card reveal">
        <h3>Disconnected from meaningful community</h3>
        <p>Healing can feel incomplete when the space lacks cultural understanding, genuine connection, and people who recognize your experience.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pull-quote">Healing should not require you to code-switch, explain your culture, or audition for belonging.</p>
    <div class="center-actions">
      <a href={base + "/experiences"} class="btn btn-on-dark">Explore Experiences</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 720px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">How we hold this space</p>
    <h2>You can be fully, unapologetically yourself here. No explaining. No performing.</h2>
    <ul class="agreement-list mx-auto" style="text-align: left; display: inline-grid; max-width: 640px;">
      <li>Come as you are. Nothing needs to be fixed, prepared, or presentable first.</li>
      <li>You set the pace. There is no pressure to share, speak, or participate in any particular way.</li>
      <li>Every space is trauma-informed and led by someone who has done her own healing work first.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint-ivory" style="background: var(--inner-light);">
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 720px;">
    <h2>Wellness that honors your whole self.</h2>
    <p class="subhead mx-auto">JBAF creates space to release what you have been carrying, reconnect with your body, and experience care rooted in culture, dignity, and community.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="col-grid-4">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Fully exhale</h3>
        <p>Release the pressure to perform and settle into a space that welcomes your whole self.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Reconnect with yourself</h3>
        <p>Use movement, breath, sound, stillness, and reflection to feel grounded and present in your body.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Heal in community</h3>
        <p>Be witnessed and supported without having to translate your experience or carry everything alone.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Practice wholeness</h3>
        <p>Develop a relationship with rest, boundaries, and alignment that can support you beyond a single experience.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="center-actions">
      <a href={base + "/experiences"} class="btn btn-secondary">Explore Experiences</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="movement">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--inner-light);">Why we exist</p>
    <h2>This is bigger than self-care.</h2>
    <p>We are reclaiming wellness as something that belongs to us. Through movement, sound, rest, ritual, research, and community, Jess Breathe &amp; Flow creates spaces where healing becomes a practice of liberation, joy, and coming home to ourselves.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 720px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">Two ways in</p>
    <h2>Where would you like to begin?</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="doors">
      <div class="door reveal">
        <h3>For You</h3>
        <p>Come as you are. Move, rest, be witnessed, and find your people.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Full Moon &amp; community healing circles</li>
          <li>Sound baths and healing meditation</li>
          <li>Yoga, private and in community</li>
          <li>1:1 coaching</li>
          <li>Retreats</li>
        </ul>
        <a href={base + "/experiences"} class="btn btn-primary">Explore Experiences</a>
      </div>
      <div class="door reveal">
        <h3>For Your Organization</h3>
        <p>Trauma-informed programs that build real trust, so your team can sustain the work together.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Organizational wellness programs</li>
          <li>Embodied leadership &amp; facilitation</li>
          <li>Trauma-informed workshops</li>
          <li>Healing circles for teams</li>
          <li>Nervous system &amp; somatic education</li>
        </ul>
        <a href={base + "/organizations"} class="btn btn-secondary">Work With JBAF</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about-preview">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">We built the space we needed too</p>
      <blockquote>We know what it is like to enter a wellness space and immediately feel the need to become smaller, quieter, or easier to understand. Some of you almost did not click because you have been disappointed before. Jess Breathe & Flow was created from that same knowing, and from the belief that healing should bring you closer to yourself.</blockquote>
      <h3>Ancient wisdom. Embodied practice. Serious scholarship.</h3>
      <p>Jessica Metayer is a 500-hour advanced-trained yoga teacher with an MS in Organization Development from Pepperdine's Graziadio Business School. Her graduate research with 15 Black executive leaders examined the hidden labor of holding it together inside systems that were never built for you. She has brought that work to teams at Workday, the International Justice Mission, the City of Lyon, and BCon, across the U.S., France, Costa Rica, and Japan.</p>
      <p class="credentials-line">500-Hour Advanced-Trained Yoga Teacher | MS, Organization Development, Pepperdine | Trauma-Informed Practice | GPS Trained Facilitator</p>
      <a href={base + "/about"} class="btn btn-primary">Meet Jess</a>
    </div>
    <div class="split-media"><img src={base + "/images/about-founding-story.jpg"} alt="Jessica smiling, seated outdoors surrounded by flowering vines" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="1800"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint-mist" id="testimonials">
  <div class="wrap center">
    <h2 style="color: var(--ivory);">What it feels like to be held here.</h2>
    <p class="subhead mx-auto" style="color: var(--ivory); opacity: 0.9;">Real reflections from people who came seeking rest, connection, movement, and space to return to themselves.</p>
    <div class="testimonial-grid">
      <div class="testimonial-card reveal">
        <p class="quote">"There is no pressure to perform or participate in any particular way. You are free to be vulnerable, to connect with others, or simply to be still and show up exactly as you are."</p>
        <p class="source">&mdash; ShanilTae, Google Review</p>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial-card reveal">
        <p class="quote">"This is exactly what was needed to recharge and get back to myself. The space was peaceful, and everyone who attended was welcoming."</p>
        <p class="source">&mdash; Jackie R., Google Review</p>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial-card reveal">
        <p class="quote">"You leave with greater clarity, emotional lightness, renewed creativity, inner peace, and a sense of alignment that continues long after the session ends."</p>
        <p class="source">&mdash; N.N., Google Review</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <a href="https://g.page/r/CQoV0PKADdZQEAI/review" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-secondary" style="border-color: var(--ivory); color: var(--ivory);">Hear From Our Community</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 720px;">
    <h2>Your homecoming can begin in three simple steps.</h2>
    <p class="subhead mx-auto">You do not need to have everything figured out before you begin.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item reveal">
        <p class="step-number">01</p>
        <h3>Choose your experience</h3>
        <p>Explore a class, healing circle, workshop, retreat, private session, or organizational offering.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-item reveal">
        <p class="step-number">02</p>
        <h3>Reserve your spot</h3>
        <p>Register online in just a few minutes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-item reveal">
        <p class="step-number">03</p>
        <h3>Arrive as you are</h3>
        <p>We will guide the experience. You only need to bring yourself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="center-actions">
      <a href={base + "/experiences"} class="btn btn-primary">Explore Experiences</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint-inner-light">
  <div class="wrap split reverse">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <h2>Healing is not about becoming someone new.</h2>
      <p>It is about returning to the self beneath the roles, expectations, and weight you have learned to carry. High-responsibility environments can quietly require continual proof, perception management, emotional labor, and responsibility for others. Over time, that hidden work can consume capacity while becoming difficult to name.</p>
      <p>JBAF brings together movement, breath, sound, stillness, story, and community to create the conditions for restoration and reconnection. This is not wellness that asks you to assimilate. It is a practice of remembering that rest, joy, connection, and wholeness have always belonged to you.</p>
      <p style="font-style: italic; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.1rem;">Healing is a homecoming.<br>You do not have to make the journey alone.</p>
      <a href={base + "/experiences"} class="btn btn-primary">Explore Experiences</a>
    </div>
    <div class="split-media"><img src={base + "/images/jessica-speaking.jpg"} alt="Jessica speaking at a community event" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="799"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="checklist" class="newsletter-section">
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 640px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">Stay connected</p>
    <h2>A little sanctuary in your inbox</h2>
    <p class="subhead mx-auto">Practices, reflections, upcoming experiences, community gatherings, and invitations to exhale. No noise, no pressure, unsubscribe any time.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap mx-auto" style="max-width: 640px;">
    <div id="fd-form-6aaca7512ac9ffd11041df36"></div>
    <noscript>
      <p class="center">Our signup form needs JavaScript to load. Email <a href="mailto:info@jessbreatheandflow.com?subject=Add%20me%20to%20the%20list">info@jessbreatheandflow.com</a> and we'll add you to the list.</p>
    </noscript>
    <p class="newsletter-fallback">Form not loading? Email <a href="mailto:info@jessbreatheandflow.com?subject=Add%20me%20to%20the%20list">info@jessbreatheandflow.com</a> and we'll add you.</p>
  </div>
</section>

